# MODEL DEFINITION & CONTEXT SPECIFICATION FILE (.mdf)
# Project: S. Mohanty & Associates — Valuation Portal & Bank Report Engine
# Format: Machine-Readable Context Definition File (MDF)
# Version: 2.4.0
# Target Model: Claude Sonnet 4.6 / Gemini 3.8 / GPT-4o

================================================================================
SECTION 1: HYPERPARAMETER & INFERENCE CONFIGURATION (TEMPERATURE CONTROL)
================================================================================

[INFERENCE_PARAMETERS]
temperature: 0.15
top_p: 0.95
presence_penalty: 0.0
frequency_penalty: 0.0
max_tokens: 8192
response_format: markdown_code_strict

[TEMPERATURE_RATIONALE]
- A low temperature (0.10 - 0.20) is strictly mandated because bank valuation reports are legal, statutory, and audit-sensitive documents.
- Any model hallucination in mathematical formulas (e.g. 80% distressed value, BUA summation, boundary alignments, or PDF cell dimensions) causes immediate statutory non-compliance.
- High precision and deterministic AST generation are required for TypeScript strict typing across all bank schemas.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: NEGATIVE CONTROLS (ANTI-PATTERNS & STRICT CONSTRAINTS — WHAT NOT TO DO)
================================================================================

[NEGATIVE_CONSTRAINTS]
1. [NO_DARK_MODE_CLASSES]:
   - DO NOT introduce any dark-mode classes (`dark:bg-*`, `dark:text-*`, `dark:border-*`, `dark:bg-slate-950`, etc.).
   - All forms must render on a clean, professional `#f8f9fa` warm neutral canvas with slate-900 typography.

2. [NO_DUPLICATE_SECTION_NUMBERING]:
   - DO NOT prefix section title strings with numbers (e.g., NEVER use `title="1. Property Details"`).
   - Use clean strings (e.g., `title="Property Details"`) and pass `number={1}` to the `<Section>` component to avoid double numbering badges (`"1 1. Property Details"`).

3. [NO_HARDCODED_FLOORS]:
   - DO NOT hardcode floor counts (e.g., only Ground and First floor).
   - Dynamic floor arrays with add/remove actions, custom floor labels (Stilt, Mezzanine, Basement, Typical Floors), and auto-summed BUA footers are required.

4. [NO_AD_HOC_NAVIGATOR_POSITIONING]:
   - DO NOT position `FloatingNavigator` on the left side or inline above content where it obscures fields.
   - It MUST always be placed on the RIGHT side as a sibling after the main `flex-1` column in a `flex flex-col xl:flex-row gap-6 items-start` layout.

5. [NO_BUCKET_MIXING]:
   - DO NOT store or upload Location Maps, Mouza Maps, Sketch Maps, or Title Deeds into the Cloud Photo Bucket.
   - Per `docs/BUCKET_ARCHITECTURE_STANDARD.md`, the Cloud Photo Bucket is strictly reserved for on-site property photographs. Maps and documents are local device uploads only.

6. [NO_UNPROTECTED_UNDER_CONSTRUCTION_VALUATION]:
   - DO NOT compute distressed value solely on 100% completion when a property is under construction (< 100%).
   - If `completionPercentage < 100%` or `isUnderConstruction` is true, the distressed value MUST be computed as 80% of `currentValueAsOnDate`, and both 100% and As-On-Date rows must be displayed in the valuation table.

7. [NO_BREAKING_STATUTORY_PDF_GRID]:
   - DO NOT alter bank-mandated PDF column widths or table geometry.
   - For Axis Bank: strictly maintain the statutory 3-column format (`Sl. No` [24pt] | `Label` [210pt] | `Value` [253pt], total printable width ~487-490pt).

8. [NO_UNCHECKED_TYPESCRIPT]:
   - DO NOT commit or deliver code without validating `npx tsc --noEmit`. Zero TypeScript errors is the mandatory baseline.

================================================================================
SECTION 3: POSITIVE CONTROLS (PRESCRIBED PATTERNS & ARCHITECTURAL RULES — WHAT TO DO)
================================================================================

[POSITIVE_PATTERNS]
1. [SOFT_CONTAINERING_SYSTEM]:
   Group form fields into thematic pastel containers with subtle 1px borders and uppercase tracking headers:
   - Blue (`border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 text-blue-800`): Initiation, Loan details, Address, Coordinates, Approvals, Undertaking.
   - Emerald (`border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/50 text-emerald-800`): Classification, Identification, Occupancy, Replacement Cost.
   - Purple (`border-purple-200 bg-purple-50/50 text-purple-800`): Boundaries (Site vs Document verification matrix).
   - Indigo (`border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50/50 text-indigo-800`): Topography, Locality Class, Infrastructure, Multi-Tier Valuation, Statutory Checklist.
   - Amber (`border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/50 text-amber-800`): Plot Demarcation, Adopted Rates, Benchmark Valuation.
   - Cyan (`border-cyan-200 bg-cyan-50/50 text-cyan-800`): Dynamic BUA Floor tables with auto-summed footers.
   - Lime (`border-lime-200 bg-lime-50/50 text-lime-800`): Land Rates & Calculation Matrices.
   - Yellow (`border-yellow-200 bg-yellow-50/50 text-yellow-800`): Remarks, Market Opinions & Observations.

2. [STANDARD_PAGE_LAYOUT]:
   ```tsx
   <div className="flex flex-col xl:flex-row gap-6 items-start animate-fade-in relative w-full bg-[#f8f9fa] min-h-screen p-4 sm:p-6 text-slate-900">
     <div className="flex-1 w-full space-y-6 min-w-0">
       <ActiveConfigBanner bankName={...} templateName={...} onReset={...} />
       {/* 1..N Soft Container Sections */}
       <ReportActionBar
         onSaveDraft={handleSaveDraft}
         onSubmit={handleSubmit}
         onPreviewPDF={handlePreviewPDF}
         onDownloadPDF={handleDownloadPDF}
         isSaving={isSaving}
         lastSaved={lastSaved}
       />
     </div>
     <FloatingNavigator sections={NAV_SECTIONS} activeSection={activeSection} />
   </div>
   ```

3. [PDF_BANK_RENDERER_INHERITANCE]:
   - All custom bank PDF renderers extend `PDFBankRenderer` located at `src/lib/banks/pdf-bank-renderer.ts`.
   - Reuse base primitives: `drawCell()`, `cellHeight()`, `wrapText()`, `sanitizeText()`, `checkPageBreak()`, and `init()`.
   - Implement dedicated Annexure engines: Geostamped Photographs Grid (2-column cards), Mouza & Location Maps stacked layout, and dedicated Sketch Map full-page view.

4. [VALUATION_MATHEMATICS]:
   - Plot Value = `Plot Area` * `Plot Rate`
   - Total Cost of Construction = `Total Approved BUA` * `Rate per sqft`
   - Total Cost As On Date = `Total Cost of Construction` * (`% Completed` / 100)
   - Current Market Value (100%) = `Plot Value` + `Total Cost of Construction`
   - Current Market Value (As On Date) = `Plot Value` + `Total Cost As On Date`
   - Distressed Value = 0.80 * (isUnderConstruction ? `Current Market Value (As On Date)` : `Current Market Value (100%)`)
   - Include manual override toggle for distressed value when required by valuer discretion.

5. [ROUTING_AND_REGISTRATION]:
   - Register all bank builders in `BuilderSelector.tsx` (`BANK_BUILDER_MAP`) using Next.js `dynamic()` lazy loading.
   - Keep `GeneralReportBuilder.tsx` as fallback and maintain wizard routing in sync with `BANK_SUB_TEMPLATES`.

